description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts there is a landed but INERT block that tries to credit compose lessons on failure. It typechecks and does nothing, because it re-implements concept-db HTTP and gets the host constant, the auth header, the body nesting and the response shape all wrong — silently, because it is fire-and-forget. Four previous repair attempts failed, the last because a multi-line anchor was reconstructed instead of copied. Both texts are therefore given below verbatim. Copy them exactly; do not paraphrase or re-indent.

Operation 1 — add this import line alongside the other sibling-resolver imports near the top of the file (the file already imports "./vessel-mitosis-cutover.js" and "./substrate-gap.js" in the same style):

import { resolveCreditPrimedConcepts } from "./credit-primed-concepts.js";

Operation 2 — in the same file, find exactly this text:

      (async () => {
        try {
          const response = await fetch(`${CONCEPT_DB_ENDPOINT}/impulses/resolve`, {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Api-Key': METABOB_API_KEY },
            body: JSON.stringify({ type: "conceptSearch", source_type: "compose_lesson", query: cls, limit: 8 }),
          });

          if (response.ok) {
            interface ConceptRow { id?: string; }
            const concepts: ConceptRow[] = await response.json();

            for (const concept of concepts) {
              if (concept.id) {
                await fetch(`${CONCEPT_DB_ENDPOINT}/usage/${concept.id}/fail`, {
                  method: 'POST',
                  headers: { 'X-Api-Key': METABOB_API_KEY },
                });
              }
            }
          }
        } catch (e) {
          // Swallow errors to avoid failing the compose
        }
      })();

and replace it with exactly this text:

      (async () => {
        try {
          const creditHeaders: Record<string, string> = { "Content-Type": "application/json" };
          const creditApiKey = process.env["METABOB_API_KEY"];
          if (creditApiKey) creditHeaders["Authorization"] = `ApiKey ${creditApiKey}`;
          const response = await fetch(`${DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT}/resolve`, {
            method: "POST",
            headers: creditHeaders,
            body: JSON.stringify({ pointer: { type: "conceptSearch", source_type: "compose_lesson", query: cls, limit: 8 } }),
            signal: AbortSignal.timeout(8_000),
          });
          if (response.ok) {
            const creditJson = (await response.json()) as { content?: Array<{ content?: string; id?: string }> };
            const creditIds = (creditJson.content ?? []).map((c) => c.id).filter((x): x is string => typeof x === "string" && x.length > 0);
            if (creditIds.length > 0) {
              await resolveCreditPrimedConcepts({ type: "credit_primed_concepts", conceptIds: creditIds, outcome: "failure" });
            }
          }
        } catch (e) {
          // Swallow errors to avoid failing the compose
        }
      })();

Change nothing else in the file. The replacement keeps the block fire-and-forget so it can never fail or delay a compose. The in-process call was verified by hand before this dispatch: invoking credit_primed_concepts with conceptIds and outcome "failure" returned {"credited":1,"errors":0} and moved times_failed from 0 to 1 on a real concept.

